{
  "requirement": "Storage and input-resolution failures return errors, rather than missing or\nstale states. A callback error is never stored as a completed judgment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations** derived from `validate_node.errors`:\n1. Input-resolution failures return errors. These are the procedure/version resolution, the node read, and the edge selection.\n2. Storage failures (load and store) return errors.\n3. These failures do not produce a \"missing\" or \"stale\" state.\n4. A callback error is never stored as a completed judgment.\n\n**Implementation shape.** I read `Validator::validate_node` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph/runtime.rs` to see which failure points exist. They are procedure resolution, the freshness check (`check_with_version`), the callback `graph.validate`, and `store_evidence`.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Version/procedure resolution failure.** `tests/validation.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` uses a procedure closure that returns `Err(\"version\")`. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"version\"))` and that the callback never started.\n- **Load failure.** The same test sets `fail_load`. It asserts `Err(Graph(\"load\"))`. Swallowing the failure as \"missing\" would run the callback and return `Ok`, so the assertion would catch it.\n- **Store failure.** The same test sets `fail_store`. It asserts `Err(Graph(\"store\"))` and that `records` is empty. The contracts test also covers a store failure after the input changed. It asserts the error, then that the previously saved judgment is still what `load_evidence` returns.\n- **Callback error not stored.** In `fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]`, the callback's input read hits a missing node and returns `Graph(\"missing\")`. The test asserts an error and an empty `records`. `fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` has a callback that asks an agent when none is configured. It asserts `NoAgentConfigured`, no records and no reads. It then adds an agent and checks that validation succeeds and stores a record.\n- **Resolution failures that could yield a stale state.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_validation_preserves_metadata_reuses_traces_and_propagates_failures]` first stores evidence. It then makes the node read fail and, separately, the edge lookup fail. For each it asserts `Err(Graph(failure))`. It also asserts that callbacks and writes are unchanged at (1, 1) and that the stored record is untouched. A stale-judgment or missing result would fail these checks.\n\nAll clauses, including the stale-versus-error distinction, have tests that exercise the failure and assert the outcome. The tests carry the `{test}` reference to the subject. I found no unacknowledged gaps.",
